    "result_text": "All tests pass. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for `POST /api/owners`. A new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` is still created, and returns `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32) read-only properties to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes them.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` columns with getters/setters.\n- **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns (tests use the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be declared).\n- **`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 new OfficeFloor function following the existing `Assign*` convention: scans existing owners for a `lastName`+`postcode` match and records the lowest matching id. It runs after `BuildOwner` and before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner isn't compared against itself, mirroring `AssignBulkSignupWarning`/`AssignNamesakeCount`.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignPossibleDuplicate` step (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `assignBulkSignupWarning` and `save`.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a non-null default mapping for `possibleDuplicate` (mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`); `possibleDuplicateOf` maps by name automatically.\n\nBecause a hard duplicate (whole `identityKey` match) is already rejected with 409 by `RequireUniqueIdentity` upstream, any surviving `lastName`+`postcode` match reaching this step is by definition a non-hard duplicate, matching the spec exactly.\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest` (the only test class; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract) \u2014 1 run, 0 failures, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
